      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable why that would be unsettling, but it's highly unlikely your smart bulbs are intentionally transmitting data or audio through light micro-flickers. These visual anomalies are usually related to power irregularities, like low voltage or interference from other electrical devices in your home. Troubleshooting potential electrical issues, such as checking your smart bulb drivers or upgrading your home's wiring, might resolve the flickering.",
